# Backend Python Services Rules

## Python Code Standards
- Follow PEP 8 style guidelines
- Use type hints for all function parameters and return values
- Use f-strings for string formatting (Python 3.6+)
- Prefer list/dict comprehensions over explicit loops when appropriate
- Use `pathlib` for file path operations instead of `os.path`

## Project Structure
- `livekit-agent/` - LiveKit audio processing service
  - `main.py` - Main application entry point
  - `api_client.py` - API client implementations
  - `recording.py` - Audio recording functionality
  - `user_data.py` - User data management
  - `requirements.txt` - Python dependencies
  - `Dockerfile` - Container configuration

## Dependencies
- Use `requirements.txt` for dependency management
- Pin specific versions for production stability
- Use virtual environments for development
- Document any system-level dependencies

## API Design
- Use FastAPI for REST APIs when applicable
- Implement proper error handling with meaningful error messages
- Use Pydantic models for request/response validation
- Follow RESTful conventions for endpoint design

## Testing
- Write unit tests for all business logic
- Use pytest for testing framework
- Mock external dependencies in tests
- Maintain good test coverage

## Logging
- Use Python's built-in logging module
- Set appropriate log levels (DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR)
- Include context information in log messages
- Use structured logging when possible

## Security
- Never hardcode secrets or API keys
- Use environment variables for configuration
- Validate all input data
- Implement proper authentication and authorization
